1
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,369
(Who is today's My Star?)

2
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:22,809
I always say this.

3
00:00:22,810 --> 00:00:24,709
He's the only one...

4
00:00:24,710 --> 00:00:25,740
in Korea...

5
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,009
who came out on top in every field.

6
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:30,250
Cha Tae Hyun is the only one.

7
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,180
I told you that.

8
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,319
I think Cha Tae Hyun is the only one in Korea...

9
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,389
(The very name he shouted out back in Season 1)

10
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:39,120
who has succeeded in everything from dramas and movies...

11
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:41,689
to variety shows and radio.

12
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:42,929
(Cha Tae Hyun is the only one who succeeded in every field.)

13
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:43,990
He was a singer as well.

14
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:45,760
He sang too.

15
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:48,830
- Right. He did everything.
- That's true.

16
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,460
Cha Tae Hyun is the only one.

17
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:52,869
There's no one like him.

18
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:55,286
(The one-of-a-kind star in Korea recognized by Grumpy Secretary)

19
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:57,639
(The morning of the day he's meeting the secretaries)

20
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,039
What's on your schedule tomorrow?

21
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,379
Is it a drama? Are you filming something?

22
00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:01,779
It's a movie. Tomorrow...

23
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:03,500
Starting from today, my schedule is packed.

24
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:05,719
I should leave at 5am tomorrow.

25
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:06,849
I should go out at 5am.

26
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:07,850
(My Star debuted 31 years ago, but his schedule is still packed.)

27
00:01:07,851 --> 00:01:09,650
My goodness.

28
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:13,890
- I'm too old for this.
- You're so busy.

29
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,459
I know. I don't know what's going on.

30
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:20,530
(His schedule is packed with all kinds of projects.)

31
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,840
(Movies)

32
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,840
(Dramas)

33
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:30,810
(Commercials)

34
00:01:31,210 --> 00:01:33,780
(Music)

35
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:37,010
(Variety shows)

36
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:39,720
He said I was like a talisman.

37
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,820
(He was cast as a talisman.)

38
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:45,720
(A lucky charm for SBS variety shows)

39
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:50,260
(The man who has claimed every title)

40
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:56,900
(Cha Tae Hyun, an industry giant)

41
00:01:58,370 --> 00:01:59,900
(Peeking)

42
00:02:00,170 --> 00:02:03,410
(He's waiting for the secretaries near the door.)

43
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:06,180
(Welcome.)

44
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:08,749
- Oh, my gosh.
- You startled me.

45
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:11,050
- You startled me.
- Why are you standing here?

46
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:13,019
(As an industry giant, he gives them a welcome like no other.)

47
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:14,820
I'm thrilled to meet you, My Star.

48
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,349
- My gosh.
- I should welcome you.

49
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:18,359
- Oh, my.
- My gosh.

50
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,589
I've only come this far to welcome you.

51
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:20,760
You have?

52
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,590
- You have?
- It's a small office.

53
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:24,499
- Oh, my.
- This is all.

54
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,659
We have another one downstairs too.

55
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,999
Nice.

56
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,170
Is this your building?

57
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:30,900
Yes, but we only use the upper floors.

58
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:33,370
That's nice.

59
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:35,809
- He owns a building.
- Oh, my.

60
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:37,110
- You own a building.
- Yes.

61
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:38,970
I can't believe I'm meeting a building owner.

62
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,409
It says "CEO Cha Tae Hyun."

63
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:44,310
Bo Young made this for me.

64
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:47,349
She made this on some variety show.

65
00:02:47,350 --> 00:02:48,666
(He's done everything and even started his own agency.)

66
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:49,690
She's not signed...

67
00:02:49,691 --> 00:02:50,989
- with your company, is she?
- No.

68
00:02:50,990 --> 00:02:52,160
It's just In Sung and me.

69
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:53,460
I saw his photo.

70
00:02:53,461 --> 00:02:55,189
- Who's next to him?
- Lim...

71
00:02:55,190 --> 00:02:56,859
He's Lim Ju Hwan.

72
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:58,330
Next is Jin Ki Joo.

73
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:59,699
Jin Ki Joo?

74
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:01,500
In Sung and I are co-CEOs.

75
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:03,229
- Jin Ki Joo?
- Jin Ki Joo?

76
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:04,269
- Jin Ki Joo?
- She was in "Teach You a Lesson."

77
00:03:04,270 --> 00:03:05,299
"Teah You a Lesson."

78
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,140
I want to meet her.

79
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:10,209
Why do you suddenly meet her?

80
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,980
I'm a fan.

81
00:03:12,610 --> 00:03:15,179
Oh, my. You've signed some great actors.

82
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:17,780
My, my. This is great.

83
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:19,949
- That chair looks expensive.
- Well...

84
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:22,149
Other people bought the furniture here for me.

85
00:03:22,150 --> 00:03:23,820
- Really? Which one?
- Yes.

86
00:03:24,150 --> 00:03:26,990
The seven chairs here, including the one you're sitting in.

87
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,330
Kang Full bought them.

88
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,590
- The cartoonist?
- Yes. Kang Full.

89
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:32,529
Do you see the table over there?

90
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:35,499
- Yoon Kyung Ho bought it.
- Kyung Ho?

91
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,969
And those chairs.

92
00:03:36,970 --> 00:03:39,669
Joon Ho bought one of them.

93
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:40,869
And Jong Min bought the other one.

94
00:03:40,870 --> 00:03:42,346
(Chair 1 bought by Kim Joon Ho, Chair 2 bought by Kim Jong Min)

95
00:03:42,370 --> 00:03:44,339
That speaker was a gift...

96
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,639
from a drama producer.

97
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,950
This television was a gift from Yum Jung Ah's husband.

98
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:51,520
You know all kinds of people.

99
00:03:51,650 --> 00:03:52,850
Downstairs,

100
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,349
on the fourth floor,

101
00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:56,449
there's a table Jae Seok bought for me.

102
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:57,796
(An office table from Yu Jae Seok)

103
00:03:57,820 --> 00:03:59,489
- Jae Seok.
- Jae Seok?

104
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:00,690
Why don't you go and bow?

105
00:04:04,630 --> 00:04:07,129
The desks were gifts...

106
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:09,230
from Kim Jong Kook, Ahn Jae Wook,

107
00:04:09,770 --> 00:04:11,940
- and Hong Kyung Min.
- My gosh.

108
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:16,269
When someone opens a new business, people usually send them flowers.

109
00:04:16,270 --> 00:04:18,510
I said I didn't need them.

110
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:20,839
That's nice.

111
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,080
(His office was completed thanks to his acquaintances.)

112
00:04:23,850 --> 00:04:25,120
Seo Jin.

113
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:26,850
I got a call saying...

114
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:29,820
that My Genie Secretary Season 2 was happening.

115
00:04:30,290 --> 00:04:32,189
Since I'm shooting "The Ballad of Us..."

116
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:33,489
- Right.
- Yes.

117
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:34,860
I told them to come to the set.

118
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,429
But each shooting...

119
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:37,730
usually takes about 15 hours.

120
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:40,600
The staff member said...

121
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,799
you wouldn't do it.

122
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,029
(The staff members said Seo Jin wouldn't do it.)

123
00:04:44,030 --> 00:04:46,140
That's what they said.

124
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,600
I...

125
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,770
But I suddenly ended up doing a concert.

126
00:04:50,970 --> 00:04:53,309
(A concert?)

127
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:55,309
(What concert?)

128
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:57,950
(My Star's schedule for today)

129
00:04:58,750 --> 00:04:59,949
(AmuttA concert)

130
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:02,620
(A band performance?)

131
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,390
(Puzzled)

132
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:08,230
(Is he in a band too?)

133
00:05:08,790 --> 00:05:09,829
Tae Hyun.

134
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:11,530
When did you form the band?

135
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,460
Well, the band was... I didn't.

136
00:05:14,670 --> 00:05:16,199
- You didn't?
- Who formed the band then?

137
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,200
- Kyung Min and Joon Hyun.
- Yes.

138
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,360
- You know Kim Joon Hyun, right?
- Yes.

139
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,740
Joon Hyun joined the band.

140
00:05:21,810 --> 00:05:23,939
- Does Kyung Min play the guitar?
- He plays the bass.

141
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:25,109
The bass guitar?

142
00:05:25,110 --> 00:05:26,710
Jeon In Hyuk of Yada.

143
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,509
Jo Jung Min, a trot singer.

144
00:05:28,510 --> 00:05:29,979
- She majored in piano.
- She's amazing.

145
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:32,280
Lastly, Cho Yeong Su, a composer.

146
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,949
(They come from completely different professions and genres.)

147
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:37,489
This is our third concert.

148
00:05:37,490 --> 00:05:40,059
- Was Busan the first stop then?
- Yes.

149
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,630
The tour started in Busan.

150
00:05:41,790 --> 00:05:44,190
They're not doing this to make profits.

151
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:45,799
They just love performing.

152
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,399
(They kicked off in Busan and continued the tour in Seoul.)

153
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,999
Everyone is doing it for their dreams.

154
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,369
(They don't ask anything.)

155
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:51,540
It's a band...

156
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:54,810
they formed just for fun,

157
00:05:55,070 --> 00:05:56,840
outside of their usual careers.

158
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:58,379
Are you just a guest vocalist then?

159
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,609
Yes, I'm a guest vocalist.

160
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:01,810
- There's another vocalist.
- Who?

161
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:03,180
Jang Hyuk.

162
00:06:03,181 --> 00:06:04,326
(Jang Hyuk is another guest vocalist.)

163
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:06,320
I like AmuttA!

164
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:10,390
This is their rule.

165
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:14,059
They don't choose professional singers...

166
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:15,330
as their vocalists.

167
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:17,030
I asked why.

168
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,900
They said they didn't want a singer who was better than them.

169
00:06:21,970 --> 00:06:22,970
(Their pride comes before vocal ability.)

170
00:06:22,971 --> 00:06:26,200
That's why I got an offer.

171
00:06:26,570 --> 00:06:27,899
So they're all singers.

172
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,240
- They're all singers.
- But...

173
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,440
don't you have more hits?

174
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,279
- You have more hits than them.
- Hits.

175
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,480
- You're right.
- You have more hits.

176
00:06:38,650 --> 00:06:40,719
- On a two-lane bridge - Right?

177
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,719
- Yes. "I Love You" was a hit too.
- Except for Yeong Su...

178
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,249
- Yes.
- Right.

179
00:06:44,250 --> 00:06:46,096
- No hit besides "Shaky Friendship."
- It kind of makes sense.

180
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,120
(Friendship shaken by a hit song)

181
00:06:47,121 --> 00:06:48,289
It kind of makes sense.

182
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:49,529
- That's his only hit.
- I have...

183
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:51,459
- two songs that reached number one.
- True.

184
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:52,829
I have three hits, including "The Two Lane Bridge."

185
00:06:52,830 --> 00:06:55,929
- He has more hits.
- You're right.

186
00:06:55,930 --> 00:06:57,050
(He actually has many hits.)

187
00:06:57,730 --> 00:07:02,740
(My Star once conquered the Korean music scene.)

188
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:06,109
("I Love You" sold 200,000 copies in just 1 week, )

189
00:07:06,110 --> 00:07:07,180
(becoming a massive hit.)

190
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:10,750
(It perfectly captured the sensibilities of the 2000s.)

191
00:07:10,910 --> 00:07:12,779
- I love Cha Tae Hyun!
- I love Cha Tae Hyun!

192
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:14,626
- Our love for Tae Hyun is agape!
- Our love for Tae Hyun is agape!

193
00:07:14,650 --> 00:07:16,566
- Entertainer Cha Tae Hyun!
- Entertainer Cha Tae Hyun!

194
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:18,796
- We'll love you til we die!
- We'll love you til we die!

195
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:20,890
(With idol-level popularity, )

196
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:24,759
(he swept the number 1 spot multiple times.)

197
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:26,429
(He even went head-to-head for the top spot...)

198
00:07:26,430 --> 00:07:28,076
(with a song that shared the same title, "I Love You.")

199
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:29,770
Two consecutive wins.

200
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:30,899
- Please love...
- Yes.

201
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,870
The quieter version of "I Love You" too.

202
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:37,809
(Every song he released was loved.)

203
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:39,439
You have three hits.

204
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,240
- After that...
- Right?

205
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:43,549
- Everyone...
- Aren't they just riding your fame?

206
00:07:43,550 --> 00:07:45,380
Is that why it's called AmuttA?

207
00:07:46,450 --> 00:07:48,519
It sounds like they want to ride your fame.

208
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:49,719
(Let's ride Tae Hyun's fame.)

209
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,350
Don't let them sway you.

210
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:52,919
- But...
- As your managers,

211
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:55,259
we need to make sure that you don't get swept up in them.

212
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:57,730
(He's wary of the band riding on his popularity.)

213
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,259
- Anyway, we held a concert.
- Okay.

214
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:01,970
There's a team that organizes concerts.

215
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:05,139
But do your concert tickets...

216
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:06,970
sell?

217
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,809
I'm curious about that too.

218
00:08:08,810 --> 00:08:09,810
(Guilty)

219
00:08:09,811 --> 00:08:11,146
- I'm curious about that too.
- Do they?

220
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:13,010
- So I... Listen.
- It's like an amateur band.

221
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:16,109
We performed at KBS Hall in Busan.

222
00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:17,879
There were 2,000 seats.

223
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,119
(Their 1st concert in Busan was a 2,000-seat show.)

224
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,519
- And...
- Was it full?

225
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,520
Not even 1,000 people came.

226
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,520
(Sighing)

227
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,650
(Solemn)

228
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:29,690
Our concert in Seoul had a capacity of 800 or 900.

229
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:30,890
It was full.

230
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,900
It means we can only sell 1,000 tickets.

231
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:36,999
We can't sell more than that.

232
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,500
- I get it.
- Got it?

233
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,070
Last time, we ended up...

234
00:08:41,810 --> 00:08:44,040
making the concert about three hours long...

235
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:46,110
because we talked so much.

236
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,180
- In the middle...
- Don't talk too much.

237
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:51,109
Some people left in the middle of the show.

238
00:08:51,110 --> 00:08:53,320
Yes. I hate it when singers talk too much.

239
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:55,720
There was an exit...

240
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:58,260
right in front of the stage.

241
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,659
- So we could see everyone...
- You could see them.

242
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:01,780
- whenever they left.
- Yes.

243
00:09:02,430 --> 00:09:06,660
(They didn't seem to stop talking.)

244
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:08,470
Don't feel bad about leaving.

245
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:15,310
(As soon as he said that, a lot of people left.)

246
00:09:16,210 --> 00:09:21,410
(They watched people leave right in front of them.)

247
00:09:21,610 --> 00:09:23,209
- That day, - You should keep it short.

248
00:09:23,210 --> 00:09:25,180
I said we shouldn't talk too much.

249
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:27,320
- Three hours is too long.
- Too long.

250
00:09:27,550 --> 00:09:28,789
Even two and a half hours is too long.

251
00:09:28,790 --> 00:09:30,219
Right. I agree.

252
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,559
I'll try to wrap up today's concert...

253
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,480
- within two and a half hours.
- No matter what.

254
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:36,990
Kyung Min talks a lot, doesn't he?

255
00:09:37,190 --> 00:09:38,359
He's very talkative.

256
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,859
(Anyone who knows him knows he talks a lot.)

257
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:43,930
Yes. We should talk with Kyung Min later.

258
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:47,730
We should tell him to stop talking nonsense.

259
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:50,110
(He'll warn him about talking too much.)

260
