520
00:19:39,830 --> 00:19:42,529
(Tae Hyun played a jockey who was gradually losing his eyesight.)

521
00:19:42,530 --> 00:19:45,599
We actually filmed at an actual racetrack on race days.

522
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:46,600
Oh, right.

523
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,169
- In Gwacheon.
- Yes.

524
00:19:48,170 --> 00:19:50,270
It was so embarrassing...

525
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:52,809
because we sometimes rode real horses,

526
00:19:52,810 --> 00:19:54,009
but sometimes,

527
00:19:54,010 --> 00:19:55,209
- we had to ride fake horses.
- Right. With the horse head.

528
00:19:55,210 --> 00:19:56,549
- It's attached to a car.
- Right.

529
00:19:56,550 --> 00:19:59,149
It only has a horse head, like a toy.

530
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:00,380
- We had to pretend.
- Right.

531
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:02,919
And we did that at an actual racetrack on a race day.

532
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:05,589
(An actual racetrack on a race day)

533
00:20:05,590 --> 00:20:07,560
It was a race day.

534
00:20:07,990 --> 00:20:09,490
During a break between races,

535
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:11,589
I rode that fake horse.

536
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:12,860
(Yeehaw)

537
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:15,599
Some of the guys at the racetrack...

538
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:18,200
started shouting.

539
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:21,800
- It was so embarrassing.
- Right. Embarrassing and awkward.

540
00:20:22,710 --> 00:20:23,750
Because of the fake horse.

541
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,139
(Today, he's riding in a luxury car instead of a fake horse.)

542
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,480
Oh, right. I heard this car has this feature.

543
00:20:30,110 --> 00:20:31,779
It has a high ground clearance.

544
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:33,580
It can handle off-road driving.

545
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:36,650
You can drive it on rough terrain.

546
00:20:36,850 --> 00:20:38,589
- The ride feels smooth too.
- Yes, it does.

547
00:20:38,590 --> 00:20:39,590
Yes.

548
00:20:39,591 --> 00:20:42,120
"I Love You" was released 20 years ago, wasn't it?

549
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:44,129
Yes. It was from my first album.

550
00:20:44,130 --> 00:20:45,699
"I Love You" is...

551
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:47,660
- Wasn't it your first song?
- Yes.

552
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,470
My wife wrote the lyrics.

553
00:20:49,930 --> 00:20:51,169
- She did?
- Yes.

554
00:20:51,170 --> 00:20:52,699
(Really?)

555
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:55,339
- I mean...
- My wife wrote most of my songs.

556
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,839
She'll get royalties then.

557
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:59,380
She still gets a little bit of money every now and then.

558
00:21:00,310 --> 00:21:01,609
She must earn a lot.

559
00:21:01,610 --> 00:21:03,479
Was she a lyricist?

560
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:04,779
No.

561
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:07,380
But she was a good writer.

562
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:11,119
I asked her to write the lyrics for the songs on my first album.

563
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:14,520
I was stuck on the lyrics,

564
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:18,790
so I asked her to write them quickly.

565
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,299
Before you married her?

566
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:21,329
Yes.

567
00:21:21,330 --> 00:21:23,030
Once I started gaining popularity,

568
00:21:23,670 --> 00:21:26,440
I couldn't publicly acknowledge my girlfriend.

569
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:28,910
- You know...
- You didn't have to.

570
00:21:30,210 --> 00:21:31,570
I couldn't make it public.

571
00:21:32,210 --> 00:21:34,179
She wrote the lyrics,

572
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:37,050
but I couldn't say they were written by my girlfriend.

573
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:39,849
So she decided to use a stage name...

574
00:21:39,850 --> 00:21:42,119
as a lyricist.

575
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:44,450
At the time, she lived near the Geomok shopping center...

576
00:21:44,820 --> 00:21:46,890
in Jamwon-dong.

577
00:21:47,290 --> 00:21:48,990
So I credited her under the name "Geomok."

578
00:21:51,430 --> 00:21:52,529
(The story behind her pen name is actually quite simple.)

579
00:21:52,530 --> 00:21:54,699
She hates that name.

580
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:55,869
Lyricist Geomok.

581
00:21:55,870 --> 00:22:00,269
(Lyrics by Geomok, as known as Tae Hyun's wife)

582
00:22:00,270 --> 00:22:02,569
Do you get together with the band members to rehearse?

583
00:22:02,570 --> 00:22:03,669
- Yes, we do.
- I see.

584
00:22:03,670 --> 00:22:06,679
But I haven't been able to rehearse for this concert...

585
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:08,610
because I came down with a bad cold.

586
00:22:09,350 --> 00:22:11,349
(He starts coughing as soon as he says that.)

587
00:22:11,350 --> 00:22:12,479
Getting a cold...

588
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:14,420
- is the worst for singing.
- Yes.

589
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,319
Today, I'll try not to use my voice...

590
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:19,059
as little as possible during rehearsal.

591
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:21,320
If I can't sing at all,

592
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:23,960
you'll have to go on stage.

593
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,660
Kwang Kyu can go.

594
00:22:27,230 --> 00:22:28,329
(My Star's true intentions are finally revealed.)

595
00:22:28,330 --> 00:22:29,850
He's a singer who released two albums.

596
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:31,930
It'll work out somehow.

597
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:34,620
You'll be able to sing the first song, at least.

598
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,769
(However)

599
00:22:36,770 --> 00:22:38,940
- How is your throat?
- It's really bad.

600
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:43,380
(My Star's condition is taking a turn for the worse.)

601
00:22:43,580 --> 00:22:45,480
(I don't think he'll be able to do it.)

602
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,850
(Please come out and stand by!)

603
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:49,549
- Should we go out?
- Yes. Let's go.

604
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:51,749
(Did his worries come true?)

605
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:54,320
(Did the secretaries go on stage for My Star?)

606
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:58,430
(He has no idea what is waiting for him. He's just excited.)

607
00:22:59,530 --> 00:23:00,830
My gosh.

608
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:02,670
There's no traffic.

609
00:23:11,570 --> 00:23:13,539
(My Star's schedule)

610
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:15,479
(Time: 2pm, Location: Concert venue, Details: Rehearsal)

611
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:16,549
(Bucheon Citizen's Hall)

612
00:23:16,550 --> 00:23:18,850
(A concert venue for AmuttA)

613
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:23,650
(They're on stage doing a soundcheck on stage.)

614
00:23:24,550 --> 00:23:26,860
- Kwang Kyu, you know where it is.
- Of course, I do.

615
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:29,560
This is basically...

616
00:23:30,430 --> 00:23:31,490
my area.

617
00:23:33,260 --> 00:23:37,700
(They came here with Nam Jin before.)

618
00:23:38,030 --> 00:23:40,899
How can you come to the same venue for the show?

619
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:41,939
I know.

620
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:44,640
- I was surprised.
- It's so funny.

621
00:23:45,610 --> 00:23:47,740
(Just trust me.)

622
00:23:48,310 --> 00:23:50,910
(Seo Jin confidently takes the lead.)

623
00:23:52,350 --> 00:23:54,049
(He heads straight in without hesitation.)

624
00:23:54,050 --> 00:23:56,590
This place feels so familiar because we've been here before.

625
00:23:56,890 --> 00:23:58,820
(Following Seo Jin)

626
00:24:00,490 --> 00:24:04,230
(They'll escort him to the waiting room without any trouble.)

627
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:06,199
It's the same waiting room, isn't it?

628
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,229
(Nam Jin also used the same waiting room.)

629
00:24:07,230 --> 00:24:09,200
- All right.
- We've been here before.

630
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:14,000
(The moment he arrives, he starts setting up his throat-care items.)

631
00:24:15,270 --> 00:24:16,810
(Sniffling)

632
00:24:18,740 --> 00:24:20,109
Gosh. The AC.

633
00:24:20,110 --> 00:24:21,110
(It's cold.)

634
00:24:21,111 --> 00:24:22,210
It's unbelievable.

635
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:26,320
(He's fighting a cold.)

636
00:24:26,580 --> 00:24:28,100
There are air conditioners everywhere.

637
00:24:28,420 --> 00:24:29,420
This is tough.

638
00:24:29,421 --> 00:24:31,420
You caught a bad cold.

639
00:24:34,120 --> 00:24:37,460
Will we catch his cold?

640
00:24:37,830 --> 00:24:40,430
Is that what you're worried about?

641
00:24:41,260 --> 00:24:43,370
(Keeping his distance from My Star)

642
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:44,800
You're unbelievable.

643
00:24:45,370 --> 00:24:47,339
(Seo Jin quietly hands over a tumbler.)

644
00:24:47,340 --> 00:24:48,370
Thank you, Seo Jin.

645
00:24:55,710 --> 00:24:58,550
(Tickling)

646
00:24:58,780 --> 00:24:59,780
(Sneezing)

647
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:05,249
Hey. My goodness.

648
00:25:05,250 --> 00:25:07,960
- You caught my cold.
- I caught your cold.

649
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:10,789
I gave it to him.

650
00:25:10,790 --> 00:25:12,329
I'm worried.

651
00:25:12,330 --> 00:25:13,399
Goodness.

652
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,860
My head hurts.

653
00:25:15,030 --> 00:25:16,499
I caught a bit of it.

654
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:18,030
Ever since I sneezed,

655
00:25:18,170 --> 00:25:21,099
I started having a runny nose.

656
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:23,270
I took all the bad luck from him.

657
00:25:23,570 --> 00:25:25,640
I think I took about half of his cold.

658
00:25:25,810 --> 00:25:29,650
(He will even take the cold from My Star.)

659
00:25:30,080 --> 00:25:31,749
Aren't you hungry Tae Hyun?

660
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:32,880
Did you eat anything?

661
00:25:33,180 --> 00:25:35,920
The rehearsal will start at 2pm.

662
00:25:37,390 --> 00:25:38,449
(There's not enough time to eat.)

663
00:25:38,450 --> 00:25:40,389
Then you'd have to eat after the rehearsal.

664
00:25:40,390 --> 00:25:41,890
I'll have to do that.

665
00:25:43,430 --> 00:25:44,830
(Staring)

666
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,159
- This...
- Tae Hyun.

667
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,360
Do you want a smoothie?

668
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:49,770
I'd love that.

669
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:51,370
Anything.

670
00:25:51,570 --> 00:25:53,370
(Shaking)

671
00:25:53,870 --> 00:25:55,799
This soy milk is...

672
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,710
also good for the scalp.

673
00:25:57,810 --> 00:26:00,340
If it's good for the scalp, we must...

674
00:26:00,810 --> 00:26:02,010
What?

675
00:26:03,550 --> 00:26:04,909
Should we rub it?

676
00:26:04,910 --> 00:26:06,679
(Should we rub the smoothie on our heads?)

677
00:26:06,680 --> 00:26:07,849
Should I give you what's left of it?

678
00:26:07,850 --> 00:26:09,290
Should I?

679
00:26:10,050 --> 00:26:11,749
Hair, hair.

680
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:13,320
(Grow, hair.)

681
00:26:14,090 --> 00:26:17,390
(Pouring the soy milk into the blender)

682
00:26:18,190 --> 00:26:20,199
Let's add a banana there.

683
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:22,930
- I'll also add some blueberries.
- You're going to add blueberries.

684
00:26:23,670 --> 00:26:29,910
(He has to satisfy My Star's hunger.)

685
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:33,809
(The nutty soy smoothie is ready.)

686
00:26:33,810 --> 00:26:35,180
(Checking the smell)

687
00:26:38,180 --> 00:26:39,420
Try it.

688
00:26:40,280 --> 00:26:41,549
Thank you.

689
00:26:41,550 --> 00:26:42,720
(Thank you.)

690
00:26:44,450 --> 00:26:46,190
Is it good? Is it okay?

691
00:26:46,260 --> 00:26:47,419
It's good. It's nutty.

692
00:26:47,420 --> 00:26:49,020
- It's really nutty.
- Is it?

693
00:26:50,060 --> 00:26:53,330
It's made with 99.7 percent black soybean extract.

694
00:26:53,630 --> 00:26:56,069
It's high in protein and fiber,

695
00:26:56,070 --> 00:26:57,499
so it's good for weight management.

696
00:26:57,500 --> 00:26:59,180
Soybeans are good for blood sugar control.

697
00:27:01,070 --> 00:27:03,640
You said soybeans are also good for the hair.

698
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:05,109
The hair?

699
00:27:05,110 --> 00:27:06,880
- It's good for hair growth.
- Hair growth.

700
00:27:07,710 --> 00:27:12,080
(Grow, hair.)

701
00:27:12,350 --> 00:27:13,720
Kwang Kyu. The bathroom.

702
00:27:14,220 --> 00:27:15,319
- The bathroom?
- On basement level one.

703
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:16,349
I...

704
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:18,310
I have a runny nose because you gave me the cold.

705
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:20,420
That's trouble.

706
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:23,190
(Thank you.)

707
00:27:25,290 --> 00:27:27,159
(Kwang Kyu accompanies him to the bathroom.)

708
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,430
Since I'm here as well...

709
00:27:28,460 --> 00:27:29,630
It's being cleaned.

710
00:27:30,770 --> 00:27:32,169
Helo.

711
00:27:32,170 --> 00:27:33,299
Can we use the bathroom?

712
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:35,220
- Please give me three minutes.
- Three minutes.

713
00:27:36,140 --> 00:27:38,010
- Hey...
- What are you craving today?

714
00:27:38,470 --> 00:27:39,539
Anything you want.

715
00:27:39,540 --> 00:27:41,179
Tell me quickly when Seo Jin's not around.

716
00:27:41,180 --> 00:27:42,910
- Goodness.
- I'll tell him later.

717
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:46,449
I'm suddenly craving soft tofu stew.

718
00:27:46,450 --> 00:27:47,619
Soft tofu stew.

719
00:27:47,620 --> 00:27:50,649
(Laughing)

720
00:27:50,650 --> 00:27:52,250
- Let's first...
- What else?

721
00:27:52,990 --> 00:27:54,290
Mapo tofu?

722
00:27:54,660 --> 00:27:56,030
Those kinds?

723
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,689
I'm craving tofu...

724
00:27:57,690 --> 00:27:59,960
and something spicy like stew.

725
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:04,699
(Tofu)

726
00:28:04,700 --> 00:28:07,200
What do you want for lunch?

727
00:28:07,740 --> 00:28:09,909
- Aren't you going to eat?
- Eating isn't our priority.

728
00:28:09,910 --> 00:28:11,350
(Lunch? We should take care of you.)

729
00:28:11,410 --> 00:28:12,440
- Earlier, - Yes?

730
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,539
I asked Kwang Kyu,

731
00:28:15,540 --> 00:28:17,380
and he said he's craving soft tofu stew.

732
00:28:19,050 --> 00:28:20,549
He wants to eat so many things.

733
00:28:20,550 --> 00:28:21,679
I asked what else he wanted,

734
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:22,790
and he said mapo tofu.

735
00:28:22,820 --> 00:28:24,119
He's craving tofu.

736
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:25,589
- He even drank that.
- Today...

737
00:28:25,590 --> 00:28:27,589
Today, he's craving tofu.

738
00:28:27,590 --> 00:28:28,689
He's craving soybeans.

739
00:28:28,690 --> 00:28:31,010
(No wonder Kwang Kyu enjoyed the soybean extract earlier.)

740
00:28:31,330 --> 00:28:32,590
Kwang Kyu...

741
00:28:32,700 --> 00:28:33,860
When did you tell him...

742
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:35,029
- that you wanted tofu?
- What?

743
00:28:35,030 --> 00:28:36,669
- Did you say you wanted tofu?
- Well...

744
00:28:36,670 --> 00:28:38,730
My Star asked me what I wanted for lunch.

745
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:41,269
I suggested them since they'd be good for the throat.

746
00:28:41,270 --> 00:28:43,551
(He suggests that soft tofu stew is good for the throat.)

747
00:28:44,210 --> 00:28:46,480
Shouldn't you have some warm broth?

748
00:28:46,710 --> 00:28:48,340
- Goodness.
- Okay.

749
00:28:48,580 --> 00:28:50,249
What do we have?

750
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:53,450
We can just order any food for delivery.

751
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:56,119
(Glancing)

752
00:28:56,120 --> 00:28:57,789
Just tell me what kind of food you want.

753
00:28:57,790 --> 00:29:02,060
(Soft tofu)

754
00:29:04,630 --> 00:29:05,690
What?

755
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:08,160
- What?
- Let's go with Korean food.

756
00:29:08,230 --> 00:29:09,399
Then...

757
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:11,099
Stir-fried spicy pork, spicy stir-fried kimchi pork,

758
00:29:11,100 --> 00:29:12,100
and grilled ribs.

759
00:29:12,101 --> 00:29:13,840
- Grilled ribs.
- Grilled ribs?

760
00:29:14,200 --> 00:29:15,339
What about soft tofu?

761
00:29:15,340 --> 00:29:17,440
(What about soft tofu?)

762
00:29:18,470 --> 00:29:19,539
Okay!

763
00:29:19,540 --> 00:29:21,080
Just wait a minute.

764
00:29:22,540 --> 00:29:24,279
Why do you keep butting in?

765
00:29:24,280 --> 00:29:25,449
He has to sing.

766
00:29:25,450 --> 00:29:27,320
He needs some energy.

767
00:29:27,620 --> 00:29:29,390
- Our My Star.
- What?

768
00:29:30,490 --> 00:29:31,519
I'll order two sets...

769
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:33,159
- of grilled ribs and seaweed soup.
- Okay.

770
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:35,336
Then two sets of stir-fried spicy pork and soft tofu stew.

771
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:36,760
(He's satisfied.)

772
00:29:37,090 --> 00:29:38,289
Plus steamed eggs.

773
00:29:38,290 --> 00:29:40,100
Steamed eggs are nice.

774
00:29:40,130 --> 00:29:41,760
I love that.

775
00:29:42,060 --> 00:29:44,400
(Thanks to Kwang Kyu, My Star gets to laugh.)

776
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:47,700
(Meanwhile, the rehearsals are going on.)

777
00:29:48,140 --> 00:29:50,370
(Actor Jang Hyuk)

778
00:29:50,910 --> 00:29:53,910
(He sings as a guest singer of AmuttA.)

779
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:58,650
(Today, he's Jang Hyuk the rocker, not the actor.)

780
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:03,390
(My Star also heads to the stage.)

781
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:06,159
(Looking around)

782
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,290
Is it here?

783
00:30:07,660 --> 00:30:09,019
(Going forward)

784
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:10,090
It's right here.

785
00:30:11,630 --> 00:30:12,659
(He escorts My Star to the stage.)

786
00:30:12,660 --> 00:30:13,800
Hello.

787
00:30:14,130 --> 00:30:15,830
Could we get a mic?

788
00:30:16,370 --> 00:30:17,630
Your mic.

789
00:30:18,130 --> 00:30:21,600
(He wanders around after escorting him.)

790
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:23,710
- Kyung Min.
- Oh, Seo Jin.

791
00:30:26,210 --> 00:30:28,280
- It's been a while.
- Yes. Have you been well?

792
00:30:28,610 --> 00:30:31,010
What kind of tough job are you here to do?

793
00:30:31,380 --> 00:30:32,780
(He's glad to see him.)

794
00:30:34,120 --> 00:30:35,720
When did you learn how to play the drum?

795
00:30:35,780 --> 00:30:37,389
- You played since you were young?
- Yes.

796
00:30:37,390 --> 00:30:38,650
You also play the guitar.

797
00:30:39,390 --> 00:30:40,919
Just a little.

798
00:30:40,920 --> 00:30:43,489
- Just a little.
- Did you improve while doing this?

799
00:30:43,490 --> 00:30:45,029
I practiced a lot.

800
00:30:45,030 --> 00:30:47,360
(Making small talk with the band members.)

801
00:30:50,270 --> 00:30:51,569
Are you feeling okay?

802
00:30:51,570 --> 00:30:53,076
- I have this around me.
- Are you all right?

803
00:30:53,100 --> 00:30:54,440
I have to try singing the songs.

804
00:30:55,340 --> 00:30:57,139
- I feel cold.
- Goodness.

805
00:30:57,140 --> 00:30:59,740
- It must be the AC.
- Yes. I'm sick from the AC.

806
00:31:00,740 --> 00:31:02,850
I kept going to the hospital.

807
00:31:03,110 --> 00:31:04,610
- That's good then.
- But...

808
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:06,079
You're a professional.

809
00:31:06,080 --> 00:31:08,920
You're a professional if you feel better on stage.

810
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:10,919
From the blackout opening...

811
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:12,750
to the transition into the first song...

812
00:31:13,460 --> 00:31:14,719
It's been a while.

813
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:16,706
(He also greets Jang Hyuk, who's been trending lately.)

814
00:31:16,730 --> 00:31:18,489
- I already greeted him.
- You already met him?

815
00:31:18,490 --> 00:31:19,890
(I'm so glad to see you like this!)

816
00:31:20,130 --> 00:31:21,660
Have you been studying English hard?

817
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:23,999
(Kwang Kyu and Jang Hyuk...)

818
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:25,569
(were on a language-learning variety show together.)

819
00:31:25,570 --> 00:31:27,739
I'm sick from the AC. I've had it for two weeks.

820
00:31:27,740 --> 00:31:28,799
Is your manager around?

821
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:30,809
- You need a receiver...
- It needs a receiver...

822
00:31:30,810 --> 00:31:32,340
to connect.

823
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:34,909
Kwang Kyu.

824
00:31:34,910 --> 00:31:36,810
- Please bring the receiver.
- Pardon?

825
00:31:36,850 --> 00:31:38,049
- Kwang Kyu...
- That's...

826
00:31:38,050 --> 00:31:40,049
- Please bring the receiver.
- Pardon?

827
00:31:40,050 --> 00:31:41,519
- The receiver.
- What's a receiver?

828
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:42,649
We need a device.

829
00:31:42,650 --> 00:31:44,490
A receiver? Okay.

830
00:31:45,350 --> 00:31:47,260
You're even doing those kind of work today?

831
00:31:47,320 --> 00:31:48,789
Of course. Just ask us.

832
00:31:48,790 --> 00:31:51,860
(Genie will get you anything.)

833
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:55,230
(He rushes to the waiting room where the box is.)

834
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:57,770
(He quickly takes the whole box.)

835
00:31:59,540 --> 00:32:00,740
Goodness.

836
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:03,109
(He messed up.)

837
00:32:03,110 --> 00:32:04,139
Goodness.

838
00:32:04,140 --> 00:32:07,580
(He looks around when there's no one around.)

839
00:32:11,610 --> 00:32:12,920
What just fell?

840
00:32:13,750 --> 00:32:16,990
(He takes everything he sees.)

841
00:32:17,820 --> 00:32:19,189
(He quickly heads back to the stage.)

842
00:32:19,190 --> 00:32:20,590
(Looking around again)

843
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:23,389
That's right.

844
00:32:23,390 --> 00:32:24,589
- Should I give this to you?
- Yes.

845
00:32:24,590 --> 00:32:25,889
(He's done taking care of the receiver.)

846
00:32:25,890 --> 00:32:27,690
- Don't you need this?
- Don't you need this?

847
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:30,270
- You can just give it to me.
- Thank you.

848
00:32:31,330 --> 00:32:33,500
(They monitor the rehearsal from the audience seats.)

849
00:32:33,870 --> 00:32:35,870
(With Jang Hyuk who has some more rehearsal left.)

850
00:32:36,070 --> 00:32:38,039
(Staring at the setlist)

851
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:40,680
Isn't "Knockin' on Heaven's Door..."

852
00:32:41,140 --> 00:32:43,510
- too much?
- But...

853
00:32:44,110 --> 00:32:47,150
We're just having fun.

854
00:32:47,450 --> 00:32:48,749
It's such...

855
00:32:48,750 --> 00:32:50,020
a great song.

856
00:32:50,350 --> 00:32:53,220
It's got a different vibe.

857
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:54,820
Don't expect too much.

858
00:32:55,460 --> 00:32:57,430
(Half excited, half worried)

859
00:32:57,560 --> 00:33:00,199
I don't think we'll get to hear the songs well...

860
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:01,900
because of the mic.

861
00:33:02,300 --> 00:33:04,169
- But this...
- Is the setup not done yet?

862
00:33:04,170 --> 00:33:06,770
- Nam Jin...
- Yes.

863
00:33:07,300 --> 00:33:11,439
Was the main act that day, so the band volumed down...

864
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:13,080
since he needed to stand out.

865
00:33:13,340 --> 00:33:14,439
This is a band.

866
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:16,579
The band sound needs to be heard.

867
00:33:16,580 --> 00:33:18,709
Since it's a band, the band has to be loud.

868
00:33:18,710 --> 00:33:19,880
(Nodding)

869
00:33:20,450 --> 00:33:22,079
(My Star is waiting behind the stage.)

870
00:33:22,080 --> 00:33:23,589
Is your throat okay?

871
00:33:23,590 --> 00:33:25,020
- Pardon?
- Is your throat okay?

872
00:33:25,450 --> 00:33:26,990
I should try singing the song.

873
00:33:27,490 --> 00:33:30,990
(The condition of My Star's voice is the key today.)

874
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:33,799
Let's begin. Let's begin with "Pierrot."

875
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:35,236
(They start the rehearsal for the first song.)

876
00:33:35,260 --> 00:33:39,470
("Pierrot Smiling at Us" performed by My Star)

877
00:33:40,840 --> 00:33:46,910
(He needs to save his voice during rehearsal for the actual show.)

878
00:33:47,980 --> 00:33:51,050
(He carefully sings the first line.)

879
00:33:56,350 --> 00:33:58,389
(He sings carefully...)

880
00:33:58,390 --> 00:34:02,620
(so he doesn't strain his voice before the actual performance.)

881
00:34:03,190 --> 00:34:06,160
(Just keep it like this!)

882
00:34:11,870 --> 00:34:14,340
Tae Hyun had a pretty bad cold.

883
00:34:15,500 --> 00:34:17,510
The weather kept changing. That's why.

884
00:34:19,210 --> 00:34:22,540
(The song slowly builds to the climax.)

885
00:34:25,450 --> 00:34:30,020
(He has to use his voice on the high notes.)

886
00:34:30,620 --> 00:34:31,989
He's straining his voice too much.

887
00:34:31,990 --> 00:34:33,260
(He's worried.)

888
00:34:37,030 --> 00:34:39,360
(A slight pitch slip)

889
00:34:39,930 --> 00:34:43,370
(Goodness)

890
00:34:44,130 --> 00:34:46,170
(Suddenly getting up)

891
00:34:46,670 --> 00:34:50,270
(Seo Genie came to the waiting room.)

892
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:55,379
(He grabs a tumbler.)

893
00:34:55,380 --> 00:34:58,709
Tae Hyun was sweating so much.

894
00:34:58,710 --> 00:35:00,380
Whether you're a singer or an actor,

895
00:35:00,780 --> 00:35:03,190
your voice is the most important thing.

896
00:35:03,450 --> 00:35:06,190
If we had enough time,

897
00:35:06,690 --> 00:35:08,559
I would have taken him...

898
00:35:08,560 --> 00:35:10,290
to get an IV drip.

899
00:35:11,030 --> 00:35:12,289
But we didn't have time.

900
00:35:12,290 --> 00:35:14,571
(He's doing the best to take care of him now with water.)

901
00:35:15,530 --> 00:35:18,170
(My Star's rehearsal is heading toward the end.)

902
00:35:18,730 --> 00:35:22,170
(He's ready to take care of him.)

903
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:25,910
Is your throat okay?

904
00:35:26,780 --> 00:35:28,980
Aren't you straining your voice too much?

905
00:35:29,410 --> 00:35:30,449
You might lose your voice.

906
00:35:30,450 --> 00:35:32,250
Isn't the song too high?

907
00:35:32,310 --> 00:35:34,049
- It is high.
- Goodness.

908
00:35:34,050 --> 00:35:36,150
I'm glad I can still sing.

909
00:35:37,220 --> 00:35:38,290
It's too high.

910
00:35:38,890 --> 00:35:40,219
Goodness...

911
00:35:40,220 --> 00:35:41,720
- What?
- Are you ready?

912
00:35:41,990 --> 00:35:43,659
I should get going.

913
00:35:43,660 --> 00:35:45,890
(They head back to the waiting room to get ready.)

914
00:35:46,390 --> 00:35:48,329
- What are you carrying?
- It's nothing.

915
00:35:48,330 --> 00:35:49,900
I'm taking my things.

916
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:52,199
Seo Jin is very worried because of you.

917
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:54,170
- Why?
- Because you might talk a lot.

918
00:35:54,770 --> 00:35:56,939
Keep talking to a minimum during the concert.

919
00:35:56,940 --> 00:35:58,969
No. I won't be talking.

920
00:35:58,970 --> 00:36:00,379
- Don't lie.
- I'm not.

921
00:36:00,380 --> 00:36:01,539
You've become quite chatty these days.

922
00:36:01,540 --> 00:36:03,040
I watched it yesterday as well.

923
00:36:03,410 --> 00:36:06,779
We have to end this in two and a half hours today.

924
00:36:06,780 --> 00:36:07,949
In two and a half hours?

925
00:36:07,950 --> 00:36:10,120
- We have to get moving.
- That won't be easy.

926
00:36:10,820 --> 00:36:12,060
That'll work if you don't talk.

927
00:36:12,250 --> 00:36:13,890
I won't talk.

928
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:16,259
- We'll trust you.
- I don't talk so much in concerts.

929
00:36:16,260 --> 00:36:18,589
You even talk a lot when you're playing golf.

930
00:36:18,590 --> 00:36:19,629
That's...

931
00:36:19,630 --> 00:36:21,229
- a show...
- Even yesterday,

932
00:36:21,230 --> 00:36:22,699
he talked the most on "Immortal Songs."

933
00:36:22,700 --> 00:36:24,829
- What are you talking about?
- Did you watch the show yesterday?

934
00:36:24,830 --> 00:36:27,240
- I watched it.
- Do you monitor my work?

935
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:28,469
It's on whenever I turn the TV on.

936
00:36:28,470 --> 00:36:30,409
We ordered food, so come and eat later.

937
00:36:30,410 --> 00:36:32,270
- Really?
- A little later.

938
00:36:32,870 --> 00:36:37,580
(My Star starts getting his makeup done.)

939
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,820
(Coughing)

940
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:49,890
Take this slowly. It's good for your throat.

941
00:36:52,230 --> 00:36:56,700
(He needs to get his voice back in shape.)

942
00:36:59,330 --> 00:37:00,569
The prince in Mongolia?

943
00:37:00,570 --> 00:37:02,099
(The secretaries and Jang Hyuk are waiting for the lunch delivery.)

944
00:37:02,100 --> 00:37:03,610
Lunch is almost here.

945
00:37:03,710 --> 00:37:04,710
In Mongolia...

946
00:37:06,010 --> 00:37:07,040
Isn't that your phone?

947
00:37:07,780 --> 00:37:08,810
Whose phone is this?

948
00:37:09,140 --> 00:37:10,679
It's Tae Hyun's.

949
00:37:10,680 --> 00:37:12,309
(My Star is getting a call.)

950
00:37:12,310 --> 00:37:13,480
It's Seol's Mom.

951
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:15,780
Who's Seol's Mom? Is she his wife?

952
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:17,319
- Should I take it to him?
- Is she his wife?

953
00:37:17,320 --> 00:37:18,719
- I think so.
- It's his wife.

954
00:37:18,720 --> 00:37:19,920
That's right. We can leave it.

955
00:37:20,120 --> 00:37:22,319
(Looking up Tae Hyun's family)

956
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:24,189
(The names of My Star's family)

957
00:37:24,190 --> 00:37:25,230
It says it's not.

958
00:37:25,690 --> 00:37:26,970
You said Seol's Mom is his wife.

959
00:37:27,430 --> 00:37:29,159
You said "mom."

960
00:37:29,160 --> 00:37:32,529
(You said "mom.")

961
00:37:32,530 --> 00:37:34,076
Don't you know the names of his children?

962
00:37:34,100 --> 00:37:35,169
It would be Soo Chan's mom.

963
00:37:35,170 --> 00:37:36,840
Soo Chan is the eldest.

964
00:37:37,170 --> 00:37:38,209
The names of the second and youngest...

965
00:37:38,210 --> 00:37:40,250
- What's the name of the youngest?
- are different.

966
00:37:42,710 --> 00:37:44,679
- What's the name of the youngest?
- He wouldn't know.

967
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:48,020
I don't know the name of the youngest.

968
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:50,520
You don't even know the names of your friend.

969
00:37:50,550 --> 00:37:52,310
- You should know.
- We're not good friends.

970
00:37:53,090 --> 00:37:54,559
We just spend time together.

971
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:55,936
(My Star's good friend says random things in all seriousness.)

972
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:58,730
You're here to make a delivery, right?

973
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:01,129
- Thank you.
- Have a good day.

974
00:38:01,130 --> 00:38:02,329
Have a good day!

975
00:38:02,330 --> 00:38:04,611
(He finally meets the soft tofu stew he was dreaming of.)

976
00:38:04,700 --> 00:38:06,670
(He opens the soft tofu stew first.)

977
00:38:07,140 --> 00:38:09,070
(Can I eat first?)

978
00:38:09,440 --> 00:38:11,339
- Give it to me.
- It's okay.

979
00:38:11,340 --> 00:38:13,169
- This...
- I took all the lids off.

980
00:38:13,170 --> 00:38:15,140
I wanted to take the lid off.

981
00:38:16,550 --> 00:38:18,049
(The table is ready.)

982
00:38:18,050 --> 00:38:19,180
Welcome back.

983
00:38:19,210 --> 00:38:21,220
(His eyes are only focused on the soft tofu stew.)

984
00:38:22,380 --> 00:38:23,449
(It's all over his finger because he was in a rush.)

985
00:38:23,450 --> 00:38:24,520
Amazing.

986
00:38:24,890 --> 00:38:26,889
The soft tofu stew is finally here.

987
00:38:26,890 --> 00:38:27,959
- Yes.
- Take a seat.

988
00:38:27,960 --> 00:38:29,590
The soft tofu stew is finally here.

989
00:38:30,330 --> 00:38:31,590
We don't have enough spoons.

990
00:38:32,060 --> 00:38:33,799
We're short on spoons only. There are enough chopsticks.

991
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:35,160
(There are 4 spoons and 6 people.)

992
00:38:35,330 --> 00:38:36,610
Didn't they give us more spoons?

993
00:38:36,770 --> 00:38:38,446
There are no spoons with the packed lunch.

994
00:38:38,470 --> 00:38:40,000
Here's rice.

995
00:38:40,140 --> 00:38:41,839
- This is stir-fried spicy pork.
- Thank you.

996
00:38:41,840 --> 00:38:42,840
(What about my spoon?)

997
00:38:43,140 --> 00:38:46,070
(He needs a spoon to eat the soft tofu stew.)

998
00:38:46,940 --> 00:38:50,180
(But he can't take My Star's spoon)

999
00:38:50,210 --> 00:38:52,409
Hold on.

1000
00:38:52,410 --> 00:38:53,580
Where are you going?

1001
00:38:54,450 --> 00:38:55,749
I'll get some spoons.

1002
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:56,789
Where will you get them from?

1003
00:38:56,790 --> 00:38:58,320
Anywhere I can.

1004
00:39:00,190 --> 00:39:01,690
Here's rice.

1005
00:39:02,860 --> 00:39:05,260
(Seo Genie takes care of the band's lunch.)

1006
00:39:05,690 --> 00:39:07,699
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you for the food.

1007
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:08,730
Right.

1008
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:15,599
Sit over there and eat comfortably.

1009
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:16,770
Kwang Kyu will be back.

1010
00:39:16,970 --> 00:39:18,109
Kwang Kyu set...

1011
00:39:18,110 --> 00:39:19,769
- the soft tofu stew here.
- He didn't.

1012
00:39:19,770 --> 00:39:21,179
- Just eat right there.
- Really?

1013
00:39:21,180 --> 00:39:22,256
(It's waiting with the plastic wrap removed.)

1014
00:39:22,280 --> 00:39:23,450
My soft tofu stew!

1015
00:39:25,710 --> 00:39:27,750
(He finds a convenience store across the road.)

1016
00:39:29,750 --> 00:39:33,050
(He's worried the soft tofu stew will get cold.)

1017
00:39:35,060 --> 00:39:37,030
(Fidgeting)

1018
00:39:37,730 --> 00:39:40,400
(The remains of the soft tofu stew in his hands)

1019
00:39:41,730 --> 00:39:44,499
It left stains on my nails.

1020
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:46,540
(Flexing with soft tofu stew instead of balsam dye)

1021
00:39:47,870 --> 00:39:52,170
(I run for my soft tofu stew.)

1022
00:39:52,570 --> 00:39:53,639
(Spoons)

1023
00:39:53,640 --> 00:39:55,910
Right. The spoons.

1024
00:39:58,110 --> 00:40:00,449
(He spends his own money for the soft tofu stew.)

1025
00:40:00,450 --> 00:40:01,780
Your payment is complete.

1026
00:40:04,420 --> 00:40:07,060
(52m to the soft tofu)

1027
00:40:09,460 --> 00:40:10,960
(Sniffing)

1028
00:40:11,990 --> 00:40:18,030
(He tries to remember the soft tofu stew with the smell.)

1029
00:40:19,370 --> 00:40:22,540
(The traffic light feels especially long today.)

1030
00:40:24,170 --> 00:40:26,009
(52m to the soft tofu)

1031
00:40:26,010 --> 00:40:29,940
(My soft tofu stew is more important than My Star right now.)

1032
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:34,680
(Running at the fastest speed ever on My Genie Secretary)

1033
00:40:36,620 --> 00:40:37,890
My soft tofu stew!

1034
00:40:39,620 --> 00:40:40,990
Sit over here.

1035
00:40:42,620 --> 00:40:44,760
(Finally getting to taste the soft tofu stew)

1036
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,470
You're really amazing.

1037
00:40:51,070 --> 00:40:53,800
I guess you really wanted to have the soft tofu stew.

1038
00:40:56,270 --> 00:40:57,340
This is it.

1039
00:40:57,640 --> 00:40:59,370
Soft tofu stew is always soft.

1040
00:40:59,740 --> 00:41:01,210
It's spicy.

1041
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:04,480
There's that softness only soft tofu has.

1042
00:41:04,810 --> 00:41:06,209
The feeling you get...

1043
00:41:06,210 --> 00:41:09,450
when that softness goes down your throat.

1044
00:41:09,950 --> 00:41:13,920
It blends with the spicy chili oil...

1045
