01:19:35,920 --> 01:19:37,459
The third was to become an actor.

1828
01:19:37,460 --> 01:19:39,489
- I see.
- So back in high school...

1829
01:19:39,490 --> 01:19:40,490
Did becoming a singer come first?

1830
01:19:40,491 --> 01:19:41,890
Yes, becoming a singer came first.

1831
01:19:42,230 --> 01:19:43,330
I could make a movie,

1832
01:19:44,130 --> 01:19:46,729
appear in it, and even sing the soundtrack for it...

1833
01:19:46,730 --> 01:19:48,630
in the future.

1834
01:19:49,140 --> 01:19:50,240
And you did in the end.

1835
01:19:50,470 --> 01:19:51,539
- You did.
- No.

1836
01:19:51,540 --> 01:19:53,486
- You even had a concert.
- The first work was...

1837
01:19:53,510 --> 01:19:54,990
You did everything besides directing.

1838
01:19:55,070 --> 01:19:56,410
I directed a drama.

1839
01:19:56,940 --> 01:19:58,640
- You did?
- Right, I remember now.

1840
01:19:59,380 --> 01:20:01,409
- Did he direct a drama?
- He did.

1841
01:20:01,410 --> 01:20:04,250
It was with Yoo Ho Jin, a director of variety shows.

1842
01:20:04,820 --> 01:20:07,119
I even directed a 16-episode-long drama.

1843
01:20:07,120 --> 01:20:08,749
- I remember.
- A 16-episode drama?

1844
01:20:08,750 --> 01:20:09,789
(Even directed a 16-episode drama)

1845
01:20:09,790 --> 01:20:11,090
Yes, I was even a director.

1846
01:20:11,360 --> 01:20:13,066
I told you he was the one and only in Korea.

1847
01:20:13,090 --> 01:20:14,090
A jack of all trades.

1848
01:20:14,330 --> 01:20:15,689
- I told you so.
- A master of all trades.

1849
01:20:15,690 --> 01:20:17,330
Yes. You see,

1850
01:20:17,760 --> 01:20:19,369
back then, I was an entertainer.

1851
01:20:19,370 --> 01:20:20,699
- I passed the entertainer exam...
- Right.

1852
01:20:20,700 --> 01:20:21,800
For KBS.

1853
01:20:22,170 --> 01:20:23,740
Class one of Super Entertainer.

1854
01:20:24,070 --> 01:20:25,739
- What year was it?
- It was 1995.

1855
01:20:25,740 --> 01:20:27,700
(Debuted in 1995 as Class 1 of Super Entertainer)

1856
01:20:28,070 --> 01:20:31,280
His specialty is singing trot while playing the drums.

1857
01:20:31,610 --> 01:20:34,349
He says his greatest strength is his incredible patience.

1858
01:20:34,350 --> 01:20:35,980
Number 50, Cha Tae Hyun.

1859
01:20:37,720 --> 01:20:41,119
(50: Cha Tae Hyun, 19 years old)

1860
01:20:41,120 --> 01:20:42,420
Number 50, the end.

1861
01:20:45,260 --> 01:20:46,559
You're my senior.

1862
01:20:46,560 --> 01:20:47,589
(Debuted in 1995)

1863
01:20:47,590 --> 01:20:48,789
- Gosh.
- He's a veteran.

1864
01:20:48,790 --> 01:20:49,959
- With the utmost respect...
- For real?

1865
01:20:49,960 --> 01:20:51,859
- Of course.
- You...

1866
01:20:51,860 --> 01:20:54,499
I'll cook the meat. I'll do it.

1867
01:20:54,500 --> 01:20:55,529
I didn't know you were a veteran.

1868
01:20:55,530 --> 01:20:56,939
(A senior who debuted 4 years earlier)

1869
01:20:56,940 --> 01:20:59,940
Many from Class of 14 are famous.

1870
01:21:00,670 --> 01:21:02,640
- Are you done, Seo Jin?
- No.

1871
01:21:03,010 --> 01:21:06,350
Seeing you not drink is so awkward, Tae Hyun.

1872
01:21:07,250 --> 01:21:09,219
Did you two have drinks before?

1873
01:21:09,220 --> 01:21:10,249
- Of course.
- Of course.

1874
01:21:10,250 --> 01:21:11,350
- Where?
- At my house.

1875
01:21:12,050 --> 01:21:13,720
You stopped drinking...

1876
01:21:14,820 --> 01:21:16,159
How long have you not drunk for?

1877
01:21:16,160 --> 01:21:17,660
- Three years.
- Three years?

1878
01:21:17,790 --> 01:21:18,959
(My Star has not been drinking for 3 years.)

1879
01:21:18,960 --> 01:21:20,730
It's not like...

1880
01:21:21,590 --> 01:21:23,800
I had a reason to quit drinking.

1881
01:21:24,330 --> 01:21:27,230
There was a time when my wife was banned...

1882
01:21:27,600 --> 01:21:30,400
from drinking for a couple of months.

1883
01:21:30,640 --> 01:21:31,769
- You?
- My wife.

1884
01:21:31,770 --> 01:21:32,809
I see.

1885
01:21:32,810 --> 01:21:34,710
She brought home non-alcoholic drinks.

1886
01:21:35,670 --> 01:21:38,240
It wasn't all that bad.

1887
01:21:38,910 --> 01:21:41,070
- The non-alcoholic drinks?
- Yes, it wasn't that bad.

1888
01:21:41,450 --> 01:21:45,150
So I took that to a drinking get-together a couple of times.

1889
01:21:46,250 --> 01:21:49,220
Just like earlier, I'd drink...

1890
01:21:50,160 --> 01:21:51,890
the first glass as is.

1891
01:21:52,220 --> 01:21:54,159
So the first glass is regular beer?

1892
01:21:54,160 --> 01:21:57,459
Whatever it may be, I drink that.

1893
01:21:57,460 --> 01:21:58,899
(The first glass is a regular alcoholic drink.)

1894
01:21:58,900 --> 01:21:59,999
Just one glass?

1895
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:01,569
- I drink that one glass.
- Okay.

1896
01:22:01,570 --> 01:22:02,999
When I move on to a non-alcoholic drink,

1897
01:22:03,000 --> 01:22:04,000
it tastes the same!

1898
01:22:04,540 --> 01:22:06,639
I feel drunk like I always would.

1899
01:22:06,640 --> 01:22:08,109
Do you still get tipsy?

1900
01:22:08,110 --> 01:22:10,709
Of course, because I still drank something.

1901
01:22:10,710 --> 01:22:11,880
He already had a glass.

1902
01:22:12,850 --> 01:22:16,119
Waking up...

1903
01:22:16,120 --> 01:22:19,149
the next day isn't tough at all.

1904
01:22:19,150 --> 01:22:20,389
- It's nice, right?
- There must be no hangover.

1905
01:22:20,390 --> 01:22:21,720
For real.

1906
01:22:22,450 --> 01:22:25,519
Because I have to drop my children off,

1907
01:22:25,520 --> 01:22:26,929
I wake up at 6:30am.

1908
01:22:26,930 --> 01:22:28,989
As I'm a morning person, I'm fine with it.

1909
01:22:28,990 --> 01:22:30,299
I'm fine with waking up early.

1910
01:22:30,300 --> 01:22:33,099
But my wife can't wake up since way before.

1911
01:22:33,100 --> 01:22:34,870
I simply need to make breakfast for them,

1912
01:22:35,100 --> 01:22:38,000
and that's just plating the food my wife already made.

1913
01:22:38,170 --> 01:22:41,710
After waking up at 6am, I make breakfast for my children,

1914
01:22:41,840 --> 01:22:42,910
drop them off,

1915
01:22:43,410 --> 01:22:45,610
and exercise during lunch.

1916
01:22:45,880 --> 01:22:48,579
That cycle makes me...

1917
01:22:48,580 --> 01:22:50,520
work out on a regular basis.

1918
01:22:51,520 --> 01:22:52,520
(The positive effects of drinking less)

1919
01:22:52,520 --> 01:22:53,520
Nice.

1920
01:22:54,390 --> 01:22:56,420
Isn't it tough in the morning after you drink?

1921
01:22:56,760 --> 01:22:58,859
It's tough. I'm in no state to do anything the next day.

1922
01:22:58,860 --> 01:23:00,659
- Right?
- Drink with him,

1923
01:23:00,660 --> 01:23:01,989
and the next day...

1924
01:23:01,990 --> 01:23:05,060
Kwang Kyu, I stop drinking. It's you who doesn't.

1925
01:23:05,460 --> 01:23:07,629
You keep threatening me to drink more...

1926
01:23:07,630 --> 01:23:08,669
when I don't.

1927
01:23:08,670 --> 01:23:10,299
But I stop midway while drinking.

1928
01:23:10,300 --> 01:23:12,070
After a hemorrhoidectomy,

1929
01:23:12,400 --> 01:23:14,610
I had non-alcoholic drinks.

1930
01:23:14,970 --> 01:23:16,539
- You did?
- He flipped out at me.

1931
01:23:16,540 --> 01:23:18,680
"A man shouldn't drink non-alcoholic drinks!"

1932
01:23:18,840 --> 01:23:20,780
I got scolded so much back then.

1933
01:23:21,650 --> 01:23:23,520
Quitting drinking is...

1934
01:23:24,020 --> 01:23:25,320
Do you work out every day?

1935
01:23:25,880 --> 01:23:27,349
I've always worked out every day.

1936
01:23:27,350 --> 01:23:28,519
I only do cardio.

1937
01:23:28,520 --> 01:23:29,619
Cardio?

1938
01:23:29,620 --> 01:23:31,389
You see, my default steps are...

1939
01:23:31,390 --> 01:23:32,990
(Let's see.)

1940
01:23:33,890 --> 01:23:36,130
The average daily steps are 13,000.

1941
01:23:37,630 --> 01:23:39,699
- What?
- It's 13,000 steps no matter what.

1942
01:23:39,700 --> 01:23:41,069
(My Star is serious about walking.)

1943
01:23:41,070 --> 01:23:42,699
- How do you do that?
- In one day?

1944
01:23:42,700 --> 01:23:43,700
(Without a single break)

1945
01:23:43,701 --> 01:23:46,339
- Thirteen thousand steps are...
- Is that the average for...

1946
01:23:46,340 --> 01:23:47,910
- not easy.
- one day?

1947
01:23:48,470 --> 01:23:50,540
Say I have a shoot in the provinces.

1948
01:23:50,940 --> 01:23:53,849
You know that portable stepper?

1949
01:23:53,850 --> 01:23:55,149
- The one you step on?
- Yes.

1950
01:23:55,150 --> 01:23:56,379
- The one you stand on?
- Yes.

1951
01:23:56,380 --> 01:23:57,650
I packed that with me.

1952
01:23:58,020 --> 01:23:59,079
I used that in the hotel.

1953
01:23:59,080 --> 01:24:01,119
- At the shoot site?
- You worked out diligently.

1954
01:24:01,120 --> 01:24:02,589
All I did was walk.

1955
01:24:02,590 --> 01:24:03,960
It was all cardio.

1956
01:24:04,090 --> 01:24:07,289
I thought it was the bare minimum...

1957
01:24:07,290 --> 01:24:08,389
- I should do.
- Amazing.

1958
01:24:08,390 --> 01:24:11,100
I broke about two steppers...

1959
01:24:11,400 --> 01:24:12,560
from using them all the time.

1960
01:24:12,970 --> 01:24:14,729
- You've always been working out.
- And...

1961
01:24:14,730 --> 01:24:16,399
- You're right.
- I had...

1962
01:24:16,400 --> 01:24:18,899
- an indoor cycling bike...
- Yes.

1963
01:24:18,900 --> 01:24:20,469
- at home, - I see.

1964
01:24:20,470 --> 01:24:23,179
And the one where you move like this on the machine.

1965
01:24:23,180 --> 01:24:24,609
- An elliptical.
- An elliptical.

1966
01:24:24,610 --> 01:24:25,770
- An elliptical.
- I had one.

1967
01:24:25,810 --> 01:24:27,750
- Your home was a gym.
- Not once...

1968
01:24:28,150 --> 01:24:30,019
- Did you miss a day?
- did I...

1969
01:24:30,020 --> 01:24:31,079
use that as...

1970
01:24:31,080 --> 01:24:32,649
- a drying rack...
- A drying rack?

1971
01:24:32,650 --> 01:24:33,749
Or anything.

1972
01:24:33,750 --> 01:24:35,719
- Not even a drying rack.
- I got the most out of them.

1973
01:24:35,720 --> 01:24:36,759
(Working out at home is incredible.)

1974
01:24:36,760 --> 01:24:38,259
Tae Hyun has always been...

1975
01:24:38,260 --> 01:24:39,660
- working out.
- Right?

1976
01:24:40,160 --> 01:24:41,490
From what I see,

1977
01:24:41,730 --> 01:24:44,000
I was able to hold out doing all sorts of work...

1978
01:24:44,160 --> 01:24:46,269
because my stamina grew from walking and such.

1979
01:24:46,270 --> 01:24:47,529
(There's a reason My Star is still active.)

1980
01:24:47,530 --> 01:24:50,100
When Soo Chan was born...

1981
01:24:50,640 --> 01:24:54,370
Soo Chan was such a light sleeper that...

1982
01:24:54,470 --> 01:24:57,380
I either had to carry him around or put him in a stroller.

1983
01:24:58,010 --> 01:25:01,250
Because I had to walk, I just took Soo Chan with me.

1984
01:25:01,510 --> 01:25:04,050
I had a morning walking route I took every day in Ichon-dong.

1985
01:25:04,680 --> 01:25:08,750
The old ladies of the neighborhood had to just spot me.

1986
01:25:09,720 --> 01:25:11,989
- A devoted husband.
- But I hate that term.

1987
01:25:11,990 --> 01:25:14,329
(The truth behind the devoted husband rumor)

1988
01:25:14,330 --> 01:25:15,460
How do I put it?

1989
01:25:15,730 --> 01:25:18,260
- The image that I'm a family man.
- Right.

1990
01:25:18,530 --> 01:25:19,829
A romantic.

1991
01:25:19,830 --> 01:25:22,200
It's giving me such a hard time, Kwang Kyu.

1992
01:25:22,600 --> 01:25:24,570
I hope people will stop saying that.

1993
01:25:25,640 --> 01:25:27,210
- I might not be one.
- The thing is,

1994
01:25:27,570 --> 01:25:29,439
you dated her since high school and even married her.

1995
01:25:29,440 --> 01:25:30,809
Only a romantic could do it.

1996
01:25:30,810 --> 01:25:32,340
No, listen.

1997
01:25:32,910 --> 01:25:34,379
That's just how...

1998
01:25:34,380 --> 01:25:36,550
things unfolded as I lived.

1999
01:25:37,450 --> 01:25:38,619
We simply...

2000
01:25:38,620 --> 01:25:41,120
continued to date and didn't break up.

2001
01:25:41,390 --> 01:25:43,460
She and I promised...

2002
01:25:43,720 --> 01:25:47,130
to get married when we turned 30.

2003
01:25:47,230 --> 01:25:48,460
But you see...

2004
01:25:48,830 --> 01:25:50,500
It's people's greed.

2005
01:25:51,400 --> 01:25:53,029
Things didn't work out after I was on a roll...

2006
01:25:53,030 --> 01:25:54,170
in my late 20s.

2007
01:25:54,400 --> 01:25:55,800
My popularity started going down.

2008
01:25:56,000 --> 01:25:57,399
- You? What didn't go well?
- Yes.

2009
01:25:57,400 --> 01:25:59,170
After "My Sassy Girl..."

2010
01:25:59,470 --> 01:26:01,540
Everyone thought he'd become bigger.

2011
01:26:02,370 --> 01:26:03,640
- But...
- Yes?

2012
01:26:04,080 --> 01:26:06,450
I had to get married at 30,

2013
01:26:06,750 --> 01:26:08,809
but I wanted one more success.

2014
01:26:08,810 --> 01:26:10,580
- Of course.
- Before getting married.

2015
01:26:10,880 --> 01:26:13,150
I wanted one big hit,

2016
01:26:13,720 --> 01:26:15,349
so I asked if we could get married at 31.

2017
01:26:15,350 --> 01:26:16,459
That was what broke us up.

2018
01:26:16,460 --> 01:26:18,790
(Asking her to get married at 31 broke us up.)

2019
01:26:19,890 --> 01:26:21,160
With your current wife?

2020
01:26:21,890 --> 01:26:23,100
She dumped me hard.

2021
01:26:23,230 --> 01:26:25,300
- What did she say back then?
- Back then...

2022
01:26:25,448 --> 01:26:27,578
My wife left for Jeju Island.

2023
01:26:28,748 --> 01:26:30,088
And so, I...

2024
01:26:30,748 --> 01:26:31,817
Did you beg for forgiveness?

2025
01:26:31,818 --> 01:26:33,058
Even though I had a shoot,

2026
01:26:33,488 --> 01:26:35,488
I cancelled it,

2027
01:26:36,628 --> 01:26:38,268
and flew over to ask for her forgiveness.

2028
01:26:38,428 --> 01:26:39,697
Did you go to Jeju Island?

2029
01:26:39,698 --> 01:26:41,597
(I want to beg for forgiveness right away.)

2030
01:26:41,598 --> 01:26:42,697
Did you go to Jeju Island?

2031
01:26:42,698 --> 01:26:44,297
I did.

2032
01:26:44,298 --> 01:26:45,797
In short, you're a romantic.

2033
01:26:45,798 --> 01:26:47,498
- You're a romantic.
- Come on.

2034
01:26:48,168 --> 01:26:49,928
If it were me, I wouldn't have followed her.

2035
01:26:50,408 --> 01:26:51,478
You...

2036
01:26:52,778 --> 01:26:55,407
(A move the romantic couldn't even think of)

2037
01:26:55,408 --> 01:26:56,977
You should've gone after her.

2038
01:26:56,978 --> 01:26:58,377
Just go. Please.

2039
01:26:58,378 --> 01:27:00,448
Had I not gone to Jeju Island back then,

2040
01:27:01,288 --> 01:27:02,447
we would've broken up.

2041
01:27:02,448 --> 01:27:04,488
- Exactly.
- Back then,

2042
01:27:04,958 --> 01:27:06,817
I thought I was going to die.

2043
01:27:06,818 --> 01:27:07,957
It was really tough.

2044
01:27:07,958 --> 01:27:09,358
That's what happened.

2045
01:27:10,528 --> 01:27:11,827
It wouldn't have lasted long.

2046
01:27:11,828 --> 01:27:14,797
If you bear the pain for about a month...

2047
01:27:14,798 --> 01:27:15,897
Why bear it?

2048
01:27:15,898 --> 01:27:17,428
You'll get over it.

2049
01:27:18,168 --> 01:27:19,868
Had you not gone to her back then,

2050
01:27:19,938 --> 01:27:21,507
you would've ended up like him.

2051
01:27:21,508 --> 01:27:23,407
- True. You're right.
- Right?

2052
01:27:23,408 --> 01:27:25,738
- That soundtrack.
- Yes.

2053
01:27:25,808 --> 01:27:27,207
- "Take this path or that one?"
- Yes.

2054
01:27:27,208 --> 01:27:28,447
- Just like "Screening Humanity."
- Yes.

2055
01:27:28,448 --> 01:27:31,148
(Cha Tae Hyun's "Screening Humanity")

2056
01:27:31,318 --> 01:27:32,377
Do I go to Jeju Island or don't?

2057
01:27:32,378 --> 01:27:33,577
Like that show with Hwi Jae?

2058
01:27:33,578 --> 01:27:34,964
(Stay and bear the pain versus Go to Jeju and apologize)

2059
01:27:34,988 --> 01:27:36,418
But why did she go to Jeju Island?

2060
01:27:36,718 --> 01:27:37,817
I don't know.

2061
01:27:37,818 --> 01:27:39,334
(Thank goodness I went to Jeju Island.)

2062
01:27:39,358 --> 01:27:40,618
Really, Kwang Kyu.

2063
01:27:41,988 --> 01:27:44,828
What's interesting is that things started working out after marriage.

2064
01:27:45,428 --> 01:27:48,068
"Scandal Makers" was after I got married.

2065
01:27:48,328 --> 01:27:50,998
- It was a huge success, right?
- My first work.

2066
01:27:51,298 --> 01:27:53,098
Since then, I was on a roll.

2067
01:27:53,338 --> 01:27:54,537
"Highway Star" was after it.

2068
01:27:54,538 --> 01:27:55,907
Those bound to succeed, succeed.

2069
01:27:55,908 --> 01:27:57,207
He's one lucky guy.

2070
01:27:57,208 --> 01:27:58,308
For real.

2071
01:27:58,538 --> 01:28:00,278
- Things just work out for him.
- Exactly.

2072
01:28:01,048 --> 01:28:03,684
Even the radio show he hosted came in first place in listenership.

2073
01:28:03,708 --> 01:28:05,318
Tae Hyun has a good hunch.

2074
01:28:05,548 --> 01:28:07,847
After "My Grumpy Secretary" aired, he texted me...

2075
01:28:07,848 --> 01:28:09,247
- about how funny it was.
- Really?

2076
01:28:09,248 --> 01:28:10,618
- Yes.
- Do you text each other?

2077
01:28:10,918 --> 01:28:11,988
Of course.

2078
01:28:12,418 --> 01:28:13,517
Treat him well.

2079
01:28:13,518 --> 01:28:14,758
- What?
- Treat him well.

2080
01:28:15,188 --> 01:28:17,027
Whatever it is, Tae Hyun will succeed.

2081
01:28:17,028 --> 01:28:18,457
- We must treat him well.
- Of course.

2082
01:28:18,458 --> 01:28:20,027
I'm indeed lucky.

2083
01:28:20,028 --> 01:28:21,728
What's wrong with us?

2084
01:28:22,268 --> 01:28:24,697
Don't clump me in with you.

2085
01:28:24,698 --> 01:28:26,968
Why do you keep saying "us?"

2086
01:28:27,438 --> 01:28:29,338
You're on the downhill as well.

2087
01:28:30,038 --> 01:28:31,737
(Here they go again.)

2088
01:28:31,738 --> 01:28:33,107
- Guys.
- I've been on...

2089
01:28:33,108 --> 01:28:35,548
- Didn't you win the Grand Prize...
- the downhill for years.

2090
01:28:35,648 --> 01:28:37,368
Because of "My Grumpy Secretary" last year?

2091
01:28:38,078 --> 01:28:42,187
(Everything's good, so stop fighting.)

2092
01:28:42,188 --> 01:28:43,518
It's great, isn't it?

2093
01:28:46,458 --> 01:28:50,687
(The leader of AmuttA stood up.)

2094
01:28:50,688 --> 01:28:52,128
Hey, guys.

2095
01:28:52,798 --> 01:28:54,597
- Yes?
- I'd like to make an announcement.

2096
01:28:54,598 --> 01:28:55,728
- Okay.
- Okay.

2097
01:28:55,868 --> 01:28:58,738
First off, great work today.

2098
01:28:58,898 --> 01:29:00,068
You see...

2099
01:29:00,338 --> 01:29:04,007
On the outside, it may seem like we were successful,

2100
01:29:04,008 --> 01:29:05,308
but there's an inside story.

2101
01:29:06,338 --> 01:29:08,277
(Information: AmuttA has many inside stories.)

2102
01:29:08,278 --> 01:29:09,547
Why do we always have...

2103
01:29:09,548 --> 01:29:10,977
- an inside story?
- There's always bad news.

2104
01:29:10,978 --> 01:29:12,248
By any chance...

2105
01:29:12,918 --> 01:29:14,277
By any chance, do we have to pitch in?

2106
01:29:14,278 --> 01:29:15,318
No.

2107
01:29:15,448 --> 01:29:17,048
You don't.

2108
01:29:17,418 --> 01:29:20,657
But just know that the pay you'll get compared to...

2109
01:29:20,658 --> 01:29:23,327
how much effort you've put in won't be on par.

2110
01:29:23,328 --> 01:29:24,997
Well, that's...

2111
01:29:24,998 --> 01:29:26,028
Here's...

2112
01:29:26,258 --> 01:29:28,567
your payment for all the hard work.

2113
01:29:28,568 --> 01:29:29,697
Thank you.

2114
01:29:29,698 --> 01:29:31,737
(Handing out the daily pay)

2115
01:29:31,738 --> 01:29:32,798
Thank you.

2116
01:29:32,868 --> 01:29:34,708
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

2117
01:29:35,368 --> 01:29:37,607
(Just like at their last concert, it comes in an envelope.)

2118
01:29:37,608 --> 01:29:39,777
(AmuttA's cash gift tradition...)

2119
01:29:39,778 --> 01:29:41,777
(has been going strong since their very first concert.)

2120
01:29:41,778 --> 01:29:43,847
- Here.
- Thank you.

2121
01:29:43,848 --> 01:29:45,178
Kyung Min.

2122
01:29:46,118 --> 01:29:48,517
I'm getting that there's a big inside story.

2123
01:29:48,518 --> 01:29:49,648
That's right.

2124
01:29:49,688 --> 01:29:50,717
(Curious about the amount)

2125
01:29:50,718 --> 01:29:52,417
- Please don't open it.
- No, it's just I...

2126
01:29:52,418 --> 01:29:54,218
- I want to go home.
- Great work.

2127
01:29:55,128 --> 01:29:58,027
- It must be one big inside story.
- Our vocalist.

2128
01:29:58,028 --> 01:29:59,528
Our main vocalist.

2129
01:29:59,828 --> 01:30:01,527
Great work today.

2130
01:30:01,528 --> 01:30:02,597
Here.

2131
01:30:02,598 --> 01:30:04,798
I even wrote a message for him.

2132
01:30:05,138 --> 01:30:07,837
"Dear AmuttA's forever first vocalist Cha Tae Hyun."

2133
01:30:07,838 --> 01:30:09,207
"It may be a humble beginning,"

2134
01:30:09,208 --> 01:30:10,667
"but the ending may be equally humble."

2135
01:30:10,668 --> 01:30:11,907
"We're sharing the profits from the AmuttA..."

2136
01:30:11,908 --> 01:30:13,207
"as a small token of our gratitude."

2137
01:30:13,208 --> 01:30:16,108
(Nice one!)

2138
01:30:16,308 --> 01:30:17,584
Great work to our main vocalist.

2139
01:30:17,608 --> 01:30:19,478
- Great work.
- Thank you.

2140
01:30:20,418 --> 01:30:22,448
(Let's see.)

2141
01:30:23,048 --> 01:30:25,358
(How much is today's daily pay?)

2142
01:30:26,218 --> 01:30:27,688
What's a relief is that...

2143
01:30:27,758 --> 01:30:29,504
there's more than enough to pay you in here.

2144
01:30:29,528 --> 01:30:30,788
(Happy)

2145
01:30:31,458 --> 01:30:32,757
(Secured the daily pay)

2146
01:30:32,758 --> 01:30:34,927
That means each of you earned over 300 dollars.

2147
01:30:34,928 --> 01:30:36,127
There's enough.

2148
01:30:36,128 --> 01:30:37,298
There's plenty enough.

2149
01:30:37,428 --> 01:30:40,737
(His eyes are fixed.)

2150
01:30:40,738 --> 01:30:41,907
Three hundred dollars.

2151
01:30:41,908 --> 01:30:43,108
(His eyes are fixed.)

2152
01:30:43,138 --> 01:30:44,777
- Great work today.
- Gosh.

2153
01:30:44,778 --> 01:30:45,937
(My Genie Secretary's 1st paycheck, 300 dollars)

2154
01:30:45,938 --> 01:30:47,077
My gosh, should I...

2155
01:30:47,078 --> 01:30:48,438
Should I really be receiving this?

2156
01:30:48,878 --> 01:30:51,418
Of course you should, Seo Jin.

2157
01:30:51,818 --> 01:30:54,517
I hope we can keep this system going.

2158
01:30:54,518 --> 01:30:57,418
(Capitalism)

2159
01:30:57,488 --> 01:30:59,128
How much are you going to give Kwang Kyu?

2160
01:30:59,218 --> 01:31:00,487
- I already gave him his.
- You did?

2161
01:31:00,488 --> 01:31:01,727
I gave him 50 dollars.

2162
01:31:01,728 --> 01:31:03,088
(I gave him 50 dollars.)

2163
01:31:03,258 --> 01:31:05,027
Do you think 50 dollars is a justifiable amount?

2164
01:31:05,028 --> 01:31:06,757
I would've given him more were it not for that,

2165
01:31:06,758 --> 01:31:07,927
like 50 dollars.

2166
01:31:07,928 --> 01:31:08,967
But Kwang Kyu...

2167
01:31:08,968 --> 01:31:10,928
earned 100 dollars with the lottery tickets.

2168
01:31:11,668 --> 01:31:13,937
I have the lottery tickets.

2169
01:31:13,938 --> 01:31:15,037
(He agrees.)

2170
01:31:15,038 --> 01:31:16,067
- He took it.
- Right.

2171
01:31:16,068 --> 01:31:17,867
- I took it.
- Wasn't it over 100 dollars?

2172
01:31:17,868 --> 01:31:19,284
- Yes, it's over 100 dollars.
- Yes.

2173
01:31:19,308 --> 01:31:21,277
Technically, we already got paid.

2174
01:31:21,278 --> 01:31:22,447
The day's pay was evenly divided.

2175
01:31:22,448 --> 01:31:24,348
- We already secured our pay.
- Exactly.

2176
01:31:24,746 --> 01:31:26,076
You know...

2177
01:31:26,876 --> 01:31:28,315
Before Kwang Kyu came...

2178
01:31:28,316 --> 01:31:30,615
I hadn't seen him in ages.

2179
01:31:30,616 --> 01:31:31,816
So I got excited today.

2180
01:31:31,916 --> 01:31:33,386
It was supposed to be...

2181
01:31:33,516 --> 01:31:35,385
a concert and performance,

2182
01:31:35,386 --> 01:31:37,156
but it turned into a variety show.

2183
01:31:37,456 --> 01:31:39,695
So my level of excitement went up!

2184
01:31:39,696 --> 01:31:42,026
(So my level of excitement went up!)

2185
01:31:42,396 --> 01:31:43,565
Was that a higher level of excitement?

2186
01:31:43,566 --> 01:31:44,865
I never once...

2187
01:31:44,866 --> 01:31:46,596
went out on stage during his turn.

2188
01:31:47,236 --> 01:31:49,365
- You get it, right?
- Why did you even come on stage?

2189
01:31:49,366 --> 01:31:52,836
I suddenly felt like I had to be entertaining.

2190
01:31:53,106 --> 01:31:54,805
He didn't take a microphone.

2191
01:31:54,806 --> 01:31:55,975
No, it was great.

2192
01:31:55,976 --> 01:31:57,856
(Received Hyuk's love with the lottery tickets)

2193
01:31:58,116 --> 01:31:59,146
Like this.

2194
01:31:59,776 --> 01:32:01,916
Please wrap it up with, "We love My Genie Secretary."

2195
01:32:02,646 --> 01:32:03,945
No way.

2196
01:32:03,946 --> 01:32:05,215
(That's so wrong.)

2197
01:32:05,216 --> 01:32:07,715
My Genie Secretary, it's day one for us!

2198
01:32:07,716 --> 01:32:09,396
(My Genie Secretary, it's day one for us!)

2199
01:32:09,886 --> 01:32:12,095
My Genie Secretary, it's day one for us!

2200
01:32:12,096 --> 01:32:14,226
(He ends on a wild note.)

2201
01:32:17,026 --> 01:32:18,736
When I checked earlier,

2202
01:32:19,566 --> 01:32:21,805
we performed for about 2.5 hours.

2203
01:32:21,806 --> 01:32:23,336
It was more than perfect.

2204
01:32:23,806 --> 01:32:26,105
No one in the audience left.

2205
01:32:26,106 --> 01:32:27,775
It was amazing. It was clean.

2206
01:32:27,776 --> 01:32:30,575
From what I see, keep this up,

2207
01:32:30,576 --> 01:32:31,675
(As the lucky charm of SBS's variety shows)

2208
01:32:31,676 --> 01:32:32,775
and people will find it funny.

2209
01:32:32,776 --> 01:32:33,776
(Clattering)

2210
01:32:34,476 --> 01:32:35,686
People are going wild.

2211
01:32:36,686 --> 01:32:38,015
They know what they're doing,

2212
01:32:38,016 --> 01:32:40,756
although I don't know what really happened.

2213
01:32:40,886 --> 01:32:42,556
Just keep this up, okay?

2214
01:32:43,026 --> 01:32:45,726
(And another member of AmuttA)

2215
01:32:47,026 --> 01:32:48,026
(Cheering)

2216
01:32:48,966 --> 01:32:52,866
(The fans were waiting for My Star to leave.)

2217
01:32:52,936 --> 01:32:53,936
Great work!

2218
01:32:53,937 --> 01:32:55,966
- My goodness.
- Goodness.

2219
01:32:56,066 --> 01:32:58,175
On the count of three, say, "I love you, Cha Tae Hyun."

2220
01:32:58,176 --> 01:32:59,236
- Okay.
- All right.

2221
01:32:59,276 --> 01:33:00,535
Cha Tae Hyun!

2222
01:33:00,536 --> 01:33:03,005
- I love you!
- I love you!

2223
01:33:03,006 --> 01:33:04,306
Me too.

2224
01:33:05,816 --> 01:33:07,276
Go, My Genie Secretary!

2225
01:33:08,646 --> 01:33:09,816
- Thank you.
- Bye.

2226
01:33:11,756 --> 01:33:16,917
(Please share some of your good luck with us, My Star.)

2227
01:33:17,105 --> 01:33:18,915
(I'm much calmer than I used to be.)

2228
01:33:20,115 --> 01:33:22,115
(Seo In Young, My Star who has completely changed)

2229
01:33:22,485 --> 01:33:23,845
(People don't change easily.)

2230
01:33:23,945 --> 01:33:25,255
(I can hear you!)

2231
01:33:25,855 --> 01:33:26,855
(I thought I'd teach them a lesson...)

2232
01:33:26,856 --> 01:33:28,376
(if they didn't take good care of me.)

2233
01:33:28,455 --> 01:33:29,984
(My Star, who's gotten even worse, )

2234
01:33:29,985 --> 01:33:32,125
(and her "redemption" begins.)

2235
01:33:32,295 --> 01:33:34,524
(Secretary Lee!)

2236
01:33:34,525 --> 01:33:36,365
(Secretary Lee!)

2237
01:33:36,425 --> 01:33:37,825
(Why does she keep calling me?)

2238
01:33:37,865 --> 01:33:38,865
(Seo Jin!)

2239
01:33:38,866 --> 01:33:40,311
(She snaps at him whenever she looks at him.)

2240
01:33:40,335 --> 01:33:42,341
(She gets angry while asking them to take care of her, )

2241
01:33:42,365 --> 01:33:44,241
(and even when giving them feedback on how they're taking care of her.)

2242
01:33:44,265 --> 01:33:46,075
(She said she had changed for the better.)

2243
01:33:46,105 --> 01:33:47,704
(His soul has left his body.)

2244
01:33:47,705 --> 01:33:49,545
(A secret mission for the two exhausted souls)

2245
01:33:49,745 --> 01:33:51,221
(Helping out with her lingerie shoot)

2246
01:33:51,245 --> 01:33:53,351
(Is it oaky for her to appear on TV dressed like that?)

2247
01:33:53,375 --> 01:33:55,175
(Forget about that and just take care of me!)

2248
01:33:55,445 --> 01:33:57,765
(I like it when you look down, but don't lower your head.)

2249
01:33:57,845 --> 01:34:01,215
(They're put through a brutal serving mission...)

2250
01:34:01,325 --> 01:34:03,785
(as they're forced to turn over a new leaf.)

2251
01:34:04,055 --> 01:34:05,271
(How much longer until the photoshoot?)

2252
01:34:05,295 --> 01:34:06,494
(Where did they go?)

2253
01:34:06,495 --> 01:34:10,265
(She's reached her limit waiting for them.)

2254
01:34:10,495 --> 01:34:14,265
(Can they stop her from completely exploding?)

2255
01:34:14,805 --> 01:34:17,105
(And...)

2256
01:34:17,605 --> 01:34:21,375
(The story from 10 years ago she finally opened up about)

2257
01:34:21,875 --> 01:34:23,105
I was a complete...

2258
01:34:23,375 --> 01:34:24,974
Right. I admit...

2259
01:34:24,975 --> 01:34:27,415
(I admit. I was pretty ridiculous back then.)

2260
01:34:29,485 --> 01:34:34,015
(My Genie Secretary)
